sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch14-06> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Within a species, cones with a given parastichy arrangement are nearly equally divided between right-handed and left-handed spiral directions (e.g. 224 versus 243 among 467 Norway spruce cones).";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Right- and left-handed parastichy directions occur about equally often";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter XIV, “On Leaf-Arrangement, or Phyllotaxis”; topic “Numbers of parastichies”. Scope: conifer cones (Norway spruce) and phyllotactic systems generally"
}
